      "command": "employee hire role:driller",
      "description": "#553 follow-up: a single driller/drill_rig cannot finish this 9-hole grid before well-being's 120-tick worker-revolt countdown completes -- sandbox-measured directly (pure command-mode engine probe, no browser): one driller starting fresh at tick 0 with full needs still only reaches 5/9 holes by the tick the crew revolts, and a `build living_quarters` early makes it WORSE (the driller detours to rest there instead of progressing, landing 0/9 holes). A second driller/drill_rig running in parallel is the strategy that actually finishes in time -- sandbox-measured landing at tick ~297 vs. revolt's tick ~333, an 8-tick margin at the tick-block sizes below. Employee #3 -- #1 is the surveyor, #2 the first driller, both hired above.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"employees\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driller\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driller\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": [
          "cash"
        ],
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 3
        }
